                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eacb9bb8-95e7-3fd2-9b85-a0acfe16ca58",
                        "entry_id": "8c489416-29de-304e-9c23-569640d08617",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Recruter via une assemblée désignant elle-même ses membres."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f88b473d-fee8-4dfa-abfa-30c2a4e523bc",
                                "sense_id": "eacb9bb8-95e7-3fd2-9b85-a0acfe16ca58",
                                "text": "Suppléant à co-opter"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f9fda38-e999-4b31-8358-f5097ec66a6a",
                                "sense_id": "eacb9bb8-95e7-3fd2-9b85-a0acfe16ca58",
                                "text": "Pour participer à la sélection de 50 heureux participants au TEDxBordeaux du 1ᵉʳ décembre, qui aura, en plus, la possibilité de co-opter un autre heureux participant, vous êtes invités à répondre à quelques questions jusqu’au 30 septembre 2012."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20ec9f06-0568-4ec5-b5fd-a1ccfe49f49a",
                                "sense_id": "eacb9bb8-95e7-3fd2-9b85-a0acfe16ca58",
                                "text": "le Conseil peut co-opter 4 membres supplémentaires sans dépasser 15 membres au total."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60971a72-0a11-46a6-a1ab-c050db0add64",
                        "source_entry_id": "8c489416-29de-304e-9c23-569640d08617",
                        "source_sense_id": "eacb9bb8-95e7-3fd2-9b85-a0acfe16ca58",
                        "target_lang_word": "co-opt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "co-opt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6037433-e521-3c64-ae49-bb4822d143a1",
                                        "entry_id": "a3b26f85-9a42-34ac-a7af-ccff7f679aa6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To elect as a fellow member of a group, such as a committee."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "378d0a4c-e963-3ce5-b797-744952bf164e",
                                        "entry_id": "a3b26f85-9a42-34ac-a7af-ccff7f679aa6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To commandeer, appropriate or take over."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37afe642-3575-4eb5-a83e-497f76efabdc",
                                                "sense_id": "378d0a4c-e963-3ce5-b797-744952bf164e",
                                                "text": "Artists' engagement with bleeding-edge tech will always have the potential to critique its destructive civil and military applications, as well as the potential to be co-opted by them—as propaganda or R&D—as the rise of the so-called knowledge economy has amply demonstrated."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5629536-8d03-3651-b3b7-9814d1fbd50a",
                                        "entry_id": "a3b26f85-9a42-34ac-a7af-ccff7f679aa6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To absorb or assimilate into an established group, movement, category, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5be88215-8c18-472e-8ac3-46c0b970add1",
                                                "sense_id": "d5629536-8d03-3651-b3b7-9814d1fbd50a",
                                                "text": "In the resolution between the culture and the counterculture, it is impossible to tell who co-opted whom, because in reality the bohemians and the bourgeois co-opted each other. They emerge from this process as bourgeois bohemians, or Bobos."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9987bad8-0845-4424-83b4-7b9dbdc7c226",
                                                "sense_id": "d5629536-8d03-3651-b3b7-9814d1fbd50a",
                                                "text": "Its opening track, Mastermind, offers one possible answer to a theoretical question about what prog rock might have sounded like in the highly unlikely event that it had co-opted Giorgio Moroder’s brand of electronic disco: nearly seven meandering, episodic minutes of unlikely chord changes […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
